# Frontend environment variables (Vite only exposes VITE_* vars to the browser).
#
# This file is documentation only — no secrets belong here, and real .env
# files are gitignored.
#
# ── Production (Vercel) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this in the Vercel dashboard:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production
# It must point at your live backend (e.g. Render), with NO trailing slash:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://medimind-hmim.onrender.com
#
# After adding/changing it, redeploy (Vite inlines env vars at build time).
#
# Note: the backend on Render (free tier) spins down when idle, so the first
# request after inactivity can take ~50s while it wakes up — this is expected.
#
# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave VITE_API_URL unset. `npm run dev` proxies /api to the backend
# (default http://127.0.0.1:8000). Override the proxy target if needed:
#
#   VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# VITE_API_URL=
